# Estimator + Sampler Walkthrough

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:nx_quantum, path: "../.."}
])
```

## Build a Circuit

```elixir
alias NxQuantum.Circuit
alias NxQuantum.Gates

circuit =
  Circuit.new(qubits: 1)
  |> Gates.ry(0, theta: Nx.tensor(0.8))
```

## Deterministic Expectation

```elixir
# checkpoint: expectation_ry_0_8
{:ok, exp} = NxQuantum.Estimator.expectation_result(circuit, observable: :pauli_z, wire: 0)
exp
```

## Seeded Sampling

```elixir
{:ok, sample} = NxQuantum.Sampler.run(circuit, shots: 512, seed: 2026)
sample
```

The same circuit, shot count, and seed give the same counts on every run. This cell records them. `Estimator` and `Sampler` emit no observability signals today (KG-27 in `docs/roadmap.md`).

```elixir
# checkpoint: sample_counts_seed_2026
sample.counts
```

## Checkpoints

Cells that start with `# checkpoint: name` are compared against recorded values by `test/nx_quantum/livebooks_test.exs`. Run `mix test.livebooks` from the repository root to check this notebook.
